@node Core Data Structure
@section Core Data Structure

el-rdf uses three hash table indices for efficient querying:
@itemize
@item
@strong{@strong{SPO}} (Subject-Predicate-Object): Primary index by subject
@item
@strong{@strong{OSP}} (Object-Subject-Predicate): Index by object for reverse lookups  
@item
@strong{@strong{POS}} (Predicate-Object-Subject): Index by predicate
@end itemize

@node Triple Storage
@section Triple Storage

Constituents of triples are:
@enumerate
@item
@strong{@strong{Lisp symbols}} (e.g. @samp{'rdfs:label}) with no bound variable or function (although you can
freely bind whatever you like to any symbol in the triple)
@item
@strong{@strong{Strings}} (e.g. @samp{"example"}) 
@item
@strong{@strong{Numbers}} (e.g. @samp{42})
@end enumerate

@node Variable System
@section Variable System

Variables are symbols starting with @samp{$} (e.g., @samp{$subject}, @samp{$predicate}). The symbol @samp{t} serves as a wildcard matching any value.

